  <div style="margin-top: 50px;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 24px;">Passive Activity Limits</h2>
    <p>Generally, you are in a passive activity if:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>You have a trade or business activity in which you do not materially participate during the tax year, or</li>
      <li>You have a rental activity, even if you do not materially participate in the activity, and you are a real estate professional.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>These terms are explained later.</p>
    <p>If you have a loss, you must determine whether the loss is passive or nonpassive. Passive activity losses are explained in the second part of this publication. After you figure out your amount of passive activity loss, you can deduct it to the extent of your passive activity income.</p>
    <p>In general, you can deduct passive activity losses only from passive activity income. You may deduct passive activity losses from nonpassive activity income only to the extent that you have passive activity income.</p>
    <p>If you have a loss, you must determine whether the loss is passive or nonpassive. Passive activity losses are explained in the second part of this publication. After you figure out your amount of passive activity loss, you can deduct it to the extent of your passive activity income.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
