<div class="page">
  <div class="section-title">Comprehensive Example</div>
  <p>The following example shows how to report <span data-field="example_description">{{ example_description }}</span>.</p>
  <p>Charles and Lily are married, file a joint return, and have combined wages of <span data-field="combined_wages">{{ combined_wages }}</span> in 2000. They have income from various sources, including passive activities, and they use Form 8582 to report their passive activity losses.</p>
  <p>Charles and Lily own a rental property, which is a passive activity. They also have an investment in a partnership, which is also a passive activity. They also have income from a business they own, which is not a passive activity.</p>
  <p>They use Form 8582 to track their passive activity income and losses. They must allocate their passive activity losses among their passive activities.</p>
  <div class="section-title">How To Report Your Passive Activity Losses</div>
  <p>Reporting your passive activities may require more than one form or schedule. The number of forms depends on the number and type of passive activities you have.</p>
  <p>You may need to use Form 8582, Schedule E, and other forms and schedules that may be required.</p>
  <div class="section-title">Step One—Completing the Passive Activity Loss Limits</div>
  <p>Charles and Lily complete the forms and schedules to determine their passive activity loss limits. They use Form 8582 to track their passive activity income and losses.</p>
  <p>They must allocate their passive activity losses among their passive activities based on the rules for determining the basis of the partnership interest.</p>
  <p>They also need to consider the at-risk rules and the passive activity loss limitations.</p>
  <div class="section-title">Step Two—Form 8582 and its Worksheets</div>
  <p>Charles and Lily complete Form 8582 and the worksheets that apply to their passive activities. They use Form 8582 to track their passive activity income and losses.</p>
  <p>They must complete Form 8582 to determine their passive activity loss limitations.</p>
  <div class="section-title">Step Three—Completing Form 8582</div>
  <p>Charles and Lily complete Part I of Form 8582 to determine their passive activity income and losses. They then complete Part II to determine their passive activity loss limitations.</p>
  <p>They must complete Part III to determine their passive activity loss limitations.</p>
</div>

